  <style is:inline>
    /* The two-slot caption CSS that this page carried is RETIRED (ADR-014).

       This block was the ORIGIN COPY. Twelve other pages copied it verbatim
       and named this page and its commit 9d81caa in their own comments.
       ADR-014 gave the caption grammar one home in public/assets/style.css,
       so the origin block and every copy come out. Each page deletes its own
       copy; this page retires the origin.

       The contract the block encoded is unchanged, and style.css now holds
       it. .fig-what states what the figure argues. .fig-limit states what the
       figure does not show. The gate fails the build on an empty .fig-limit.
       The quiet voice is a token and never opacity (ADR-009).

       One plate grammar, three plates (ADR-004, ADR-013). Page-scoped.

       The plate width is no longer this page's business. The figure ladder in
       style.css caps a plate at --fig-plate. The plate therefore renders at
       about 1.48x on a wide screen, and at 272px in a 320px viewport. That is
       a render scale of about 1.05, so a declared 9px renders above the 9px
       microtext floor. The local max-width: 260px is deleted for two reasons.
       It lost to the ladder on specificity, and it stated a scale the page no
       longer holds.

       The shared parts carry a `ca-` prefix and the marker ids carry a digit
       (`ca2-arrow`, `ca3-arrow`). A marker id is global to the document and a
       duplicate repaints the wrong arrow head, which no gate sees. A class in
       this block is only ever read on this page, so the digit buys nothing
       there and the shared grammar is worth more.

       Two hues only. Oxide (--accent-warm) marks the two commands that walked
       past the guard, inside a card the page already marks as a reversal.
       Everything else stays ink and muted, because a tradeoff is not a
       reversal (the .lab-topo rule on netops-lab records the same split).
       Every state is a word plus a shape, so colour is second: no glyph on
       this site can carry a state, and Geist has no italic cut. SVG text
       inherits from <body>, so every text class names its own font. */
    .ca-plate .ca-box {
      fill: var(--bg);
      stroke: var(--stroke-figure);
      stroke-width: 1;
    }
    /* An outline written as a path, so a segment can be left out. The gap is
       the claim in ca2-bypass, and an absent segment is the only honest way
       to show one. */
    .ca-plate .ca-open {
      fill: none;
      stroke: var(--stroke-figure);
      stroke-width: 1;
    }
    /* The file exists and nothing reads it. Dashed, not absent. */
    .ca-plate .ca-box-dead {
      fill: none;
      stroke: var(--muted);
      stroke-width: 1;
      stroke-dasharray: 3 3;
    }
    .ca-plate .ca-lane {
      fill: var(--muted);
      font-family: var(--font);
      font-size: 10px;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    }
    .ca-plate .ca-title {
      fill: var(--text);
      font-family: var(--font);
      font-size: 11px;
      font-weight: 500;
    }
    /* 9px, not 8px: the microtext floor (CLAUDE.md, ADR-014 section 5). The
       declared unit rises and the plate keeps its 1:1-or-better render scale.
       The floor therefore holds at every width, and not only under a
       breakpoint. The floor costs room: a 76-wide cell in ca1-costs now holds
       about twelve mono characters on one line rather than about fourteen. */
    .ca-plate .ca-micro {
      fill: var(--muted);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 9px;
    }
    .ca-plate .ca-cmd {
      fill: var(--accent-warm);
      font-family: var(--mono);
      font-size: 9px;
      font-weight: 500;
    }
    .ca-plate .ca-edge {
      fill: none;
      stroke: var(--muted);
      stroke-width: 1.5;
    }
    .ca-plate .ca-edge-dead {
      fill: none;
      stroke: var(--muted);
      stroke-width: 1.5;
      stroke-dasharray: 3 3;
    }
    .ca-plate .ca-edge-out {
      fill: none;
      stroke: var(--accent-warm);
      stroke-width: 1.5;
    }
    .ca-plate marker path { fill: var(--muted); }
    .ca-plate marker path.ca-head-out { fill: var(--accent-warm); }
