  <main class="wrap article-body" id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <a class="back" href="../index.html">&larr; Back</a>
    <h1>Context Architecture</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">The payload my agent sessions load before they open a source file. I scored it against five published criteria. Three failed.</p>

    <h2>The resident payload</h2>

    <p>
      Every session I start reads a fixed payload first. The payload holds an
      index of about sixty memories and eight rule files. It also holds the
      working agreement for the repository it landed in, and a list of skill
      descriptions. The session opens a source file only after all of that.
    </p>

    <p>
      The payload accreted, one &ldquo;remember this&rdquo; at a time. It grew
      over months and across five agent vendors. Nothing crashed. The payload
      just got bigger, and a bigger payload is not free in three currencies.
    </p>

    <!-- ca1-costs. The page's thesis, shown as geometry.

