         0 0 260 72, three 76-wide cells at x=2, 92, and 182, rx 2. The page
         inherits the site's three-cell grammar instead of inventing one.

         Two deliberate changes. The arrows are gone, because the three costs
         are parallel and not a sequence, and an arrow would state an order
         the prose never claims. The cell is 44 tall rather than 40, because a
         mechanism needs two micro lines: one line of Geist Mono at 9px holds
         about twelve characters inside a 76-wide cell.

         No digit (ADR-013). The counts stay in the prose and in the caption,
         where a reader can check them. No oxide: nothing here was taken back.

         Plate 01 of three, in reading order. The label is an in-flow span
         with a hand-authored digit (PL-3, PL-4), never a CSS counter. The
         kind is Plate and a plate sits on the spine (ADR-014). -->
